<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.7.1: Evaluating Variable Expressions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02443</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.7.1: Evaluating Variable Expressions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>c172c1d4-2c5b-4310-8d59-d9a9105758f8</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Evaluate each expression for \(a=9\), \(b=-5\), and \(c=-2\).</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="2ce28f30-9311-45ec-8259-4a441abd6f6b"><problem><para>
      <para>\(-b\)</para>
      <para>Enter the value of \(-b\). </para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>5</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 5: \(-(-5)=5\).</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="7335966d-dc58-4542-a715-339e24f82cd1"><problem><para>
      <para><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> answers for \(-b \pm \sqrt{a}\).</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>["2", "8"]</para><para>
      <para>The correct answers are 2 and 8: \(-(-5)+\sqrt{9}=5+3=8\) and \(-(-5)-\sqrt{9}=5-3=2\)</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
